.TH P3M-FIND 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-find \- parallel find
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-find
.RI [ P3M\-OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ...]
.RI [ EXPRESSION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-find
searches directory trees in parallel with a
.BR find (1)-style
expression.
With no
.IR PATH ,
the current directory is searched; with no
.IR EXPRESSION ,
everything matches.
Matches are printed as CSV (a
.I path
header and one row per match) or NUL-separated with
.BR \-print0 .
.PP
The classic grammar (including implicit
.BR \-a ,
short-circuit evaluation and find's interval semantics for time tests) is
supported.
.BR stat (2)
is lazy: tests that need it trigger it once per entry, so name-only searches
issue no
.B stat
calls.
.PP
.B p3m-find
is read-only by design: there is deliberately no
.B \-delete
or
.BR \-exec .
Pipe matches to
.BR "xargs \-0" ,
or feed them to
.BR p3m\-rm (1)
or
.BR p3m\-ch (1).
Symbolic links are never followed.
.SH P3M OPTIONS
These must appear before any
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write matches to
.I FILE
and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the listing; progress and the summary (with the match count) are
still shown.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH TESTS
.TP
.BR \-name " \fIP\fR, " \-iname " \fIP\fR"
Glob on the entry name (\fBi\fR: case-insensitive).
.TP
.BR \-path " \fIP\fR, " \-ipath " \fIP\fR"
Glob on the full path.
.TP
.BR \-regex " \fIP\fR, " \-iregex " \fIP\fR"
POSIX extended regular expression, anchored to the whole path.
.TP
.BI \-type " T" [, T ...]
One or more of
.BR f " (file), " d " (directory), " l " (symlink), " b ", " c ", " p ", " s .
Combinable, for example
.BR "\-type f,l" .
.TP
.BR \-size " [+\-]\fIN\fR[bckMG]"
Size rounded up to the unit, as with
.BR find (1)
(default
.BR b ).
.TP
.BR \-mtime ", " \-atime ", " \-ctime " [+\-]\fIN\fR"
Age in 24-hour units.
.TP
.BR \-mmin ", " \-amin ", " \-cmin " [+\-]\fIN\fR"
Age in minutes.
.TP
.BI \-newer " FILE"
Modified more recently than
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-user " U" ", " \-group " G"
Owner or group, by name or numeric id.
.TP
.BR \-perm " [\-|/]\fIOCTAL\fR"
Exact mode, all of the bits (\fB\-\fR prefix), or any of the bits (\fB/\fR
prefix).
.TP
.B \-empty
Empty regular file or directory.
.TP
.BI \-mindepth " N" ", " \-maxdepth " N"
Depth limits; the
.I PATH
itself is depth 0.
.TP
.B \-print0
NUL-separated output for
.BR "xargs \-0" .
.SH OPERATORS
In decreasing order of precedence:
.TP
.BI ( " EXPR " )
Grouping.
.TP
.BI ! " EXPR" ", " \-not " EXPR"
Negation.
.TP
.IB EXPR " " EXPR ", " EXPR " \-a " EXPR
Conjunction (the default between adjacent expressions).
.TP
.IB EXPR " \-o " EXPR
Disjunction.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
p3m\-find /var/log \-name '*.log' \-mtime +30
p3m\-find /data \-type f \-size +1G
p3m\-find \-\-print0 /scratch \-name 'tmp\-*' | xargs \-0 \-r du \-ch
p3m\-find \-q /data \-type f \-newer /data/.last\-backup
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-ls (1),
.BR p3m\-rm (1),
.BR find (1)
